{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"860165485579337779","content":"\"For now it seems like it might have something to do with 'hope', whomever that might represent. Apgan and Johnathan have been lighting the lanterns in Kingsbridge since the attack, and had some magic stones that brought us back from nearly losing ourselves to the Noir, when we called out to one another for hope. Someone might have approached them there while they were on that job.\"","created_at":"2021-07-20T18:02:58.732000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867104315071004682","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"860165485579337779","content":"\"I'm just wondering, if they were in Kingsbridge, why Hampstead's cornerstone, not Kingsbridge's?\"","created_at":"2021-07-20T18:03:38.942000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867104483724886026","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
